# IMPL-WININFO_ENUMERATE essence pseudocode

// [IMPL-WININFO_ENUMERATE] [ARCH-WININFO_MACOS_COREGRAPHICS] [REQ-WININFO_OPEN_WINDOWS]
// Enumerate macOS windows via CoreGraphics and parse CFDictionary records into domain models.
PROCEDURE LIST_RAW_WINDOWS
  PRE: runtime GOOS is darwin and GUI window server is available
  INPUT: include_offscreen boolean (default false)
  CONTROL: IF include_offscreen THEN options = kCGWindowListOptionAll | kCGWindowListExcludeDesktopElements
           ELSE options = kCGWindowListOptionOnScreenOnly | kCGWindowListExcludeDesktopElements
  DATA: raw_list = CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo(options, kCGNullWindowID)
  POST: raw_list is non-nil CFArray or FAILURE_MODES fires
  EFFECTS: returns slice of parsed Window values (may be empty)
  FAILURE_MODES:
    - window server unavailable (raw_list is NULL) -> return error "no window server"
    - CG call fails -> return wrapped error

// [IMPL-WININFO_ENUMERATE] [ARCH-WININFO_MACOS_COREGRAPHICS] [REQ-WININFO_OPEN_WINDOWS]
PROCEDURE PARSE_CG_DICTIONARY
  PRE: dict is CFDictionary from CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo entry
  INPUT: dict
  DATA: extract kCGWindowNumber, kCGWindowOwnerPID, kCGWindowOwnerName, kCGWindowName,
        kCGWindowBounds (X,Y,Width,Height), kCGWindowLayer, kCGWindowIsOnscreen
  POST: Window struct populated or entry skipped when bounds missing
  EFFECTS: one Window value or skip malformed entry (WININFO_DEBUG logs skip count)
  FAILURE_MODES: missing bounds -> skip entry, continue enumeration
